# Day 49 – Build Personal AI Playbook

## 60 Days of Claude AI Challenge

### Project Overview
Today I built a Personal AI Playbook using Claude AI. The goal was to transform recurring AI use cases into reusable and personalized workflow systems instead of relying on one-off prompts.

### What I Built
- A personalized AI workflow library
- Modular prompt building blocks
- A Prompt Builder for assembling reusable prompts
- An Autonomous Loop Builder
- Workflow saving, searching, and favoriting features
- A self-explanatory and user-friendly interface

### Key Learnings
- Modular Prompt Design: Breaking prompts into reusable blocks such as role, objective, context, and constraints.
- Autonomous Loop Prompts: Turning one-shot prompts into self-evaluating and iterative workflows.
- Personalization: Building AI systems based on real roles, use cases, tools, and bottlenecks.
- Self-Explanatory UX: Designing interfaces that are easy to understand and use.

### Tools Used
- Claude AI
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- GitHub

### Conclusion
Day 49 helped me understand how recurring AI tasks can be transformed into structured, reusable workflow systems. Instead of writing prompts from scratch every time, a Personal AI Playbook can make AI workflows more organized, consistent, and scalable.

